================================================================================
RosettaSciIO (the oracle, and the rules the adapters port)
================================================================================

Sources/FormatoEMPAD/FormatoEMPAD.swift ports rsciio/empad/_api.py at the same
pinned commit below (GPL-3.0-or-later): frame layout, shapes, calibrations and
metadata. The app's EMPADReader in VendorRawReaders.swift was read as the seed;
the implementation uses FormatoCore and a read-only mmap. Synthetic fixtures
and full-byte oracle pins are generated by tools/empad/generate.py.

The DM and Velox signal adapters (Sources/FormatoDM/DMSignals.swift, Sources/
FormatoEMD/VeloxImageSignals.swift) port RosettaSciIO's file readers' rules for
shapes, axes, names, navigation, signal types and the mapped metadata
(rsciio/digitalmicrograph/_api.py, rsciio/emd/_emd_velox.py, rsciio/utils/
_units.py at commit 049e7d7070e84779b499adaf3295beee9facb004), and every reader
is compared with RosettaSciIO's reading of the same files (tools/dm-velox-pins/pins.py).
The Velox reader moved from SpectroKit follows RosettaSciIO's reading of the
format too. Tests/FormatoDMTests/Fixtures/rsciio-EELS_SI.dm4 is RosettaSciIO's
public test file rsciio/tests/data/digitalmicrograph/3D/EELS_SI.dm4 (sha256
f9b8203f384cc355437594b649d4ea3a12cddeb231ebb65508a841a379fa171a), copied byte
for byte; the JSON pins under Tests/FormatoCoreTests/Fixtures are RosettaSciIO's
readings of its public test files.
Tests/FormatoDMTests/Fixtures/rsciio-MonoCL_spectrum-ccd.dm4 and
Tests/FormatoDMTests/Fixtures/rsciio-MonarcCL_spectrum-ccd.dm4 are RosettaSciIO's
public test files rsciio/tests/data/digitalmicrograph/1D/test-MonoCL_spectrum-ccd.dm4
(sha256 bcf857ca89b99852fe083988433b92726004c9807f519d72cb3ee978f1e6c35a) and
test-MonarcCL_spectrum-ccd.dm4 (sha256
716e4aa36615de43ec7f13098157f647dbeabebff872645fd1f49724189eb174), copied byte
for byte; the bytes are the same at the pinned commit above and at commit
8363d244a6405dfb68a545c47260648056c4b465, where they were fetched. The camera
pixel pitch (Sources/FormatoDM/AcquisitionMetadataDM.swift) follows the mapping
of Acquisition.Device.CCD.Pixel Size (um) to Detector.pixel_size, the same line
at both commits.

